{
  "name": "Hunter",
  "type": "class",
  "img": "icons/weapons/bows/shortbow-recurve-yellow-blue.webp",
  "system": {
    "description": "<p><strong>I will look for you, I will find you, and I will kill you.</strong></p><p><em>—Liam Neeson, Taken</em></p><p>Keepers of the old way, hunters are survival experts that specialize in exploiting their enemies’ weaknesses.</p><h3>Iconic Hunters</h3><ul><li><strong>Aloy</strong>, <em>Horizon</em></li><li><strong>Aragorn</strong>, <em>The Lord of the Rings</em></li><li><strong>Samus Aran</strong>, <em>Metroid</em></li><li><strong>San</strong>, <em>Princess Mononoke</em></li></ul><h3>Playing Hunter</h3><p>The hunter is a low defense, high-crit striker. They can be built for Melee or Ranged positions.</p><p><strong>Action:</strong> Attack<br /><strong>Move:</strong> Midline/Backline<br /><strong>Starting Pack:</strong> Scout or Warrior<br /><strong>Key Stat:</strong> Awareness<br /><strong>Complexity:</strong> ★★☆☆☆<br /><strong>Training:</strong> Melee, Ranged, Survival</p><h3>Class Features</h3><table class=\"NormalTable\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Level</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Features</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>1st</p></td><td><p>Hunter’s Mark, Survivalist</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>2nd</p></td><td><p>Rover (5’)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>3rd</p></td><td><p>Perk</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>4th</p></td><td><p>Lethal Precision (+1 damage)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>5th</p></td><td><p>Perk</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>6th</p></td><td><p>Rover (10’), Killer Instinct</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>7th</p></td><td><p>Perk</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>8th</p></td><td><p>Lethal Precision (+2 damage)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>9th</p></td><td><p>Perk</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>10th</p></td><td><p>Rover (15’), Apex Predator</p></td></tr></tbody></table>",
    "isSpellcaster": false,
    "levelFeatures": [
      {
        "level": 1,
        "name": "Hunter’s Mark",
        "description": "<p>You can choose a Target when you attack it or by skipping your Move, declaring it as your Mark until you declare a new Mark. The following rules apply while you have a Mark:</p><ul><li><p>Your attacks against it with Weapons that have the Keen or Vicious property also have the other property, and Crit if a Bonus causes the result to exceed your Crit range.</p></li><li><p>You roll two d20s on Checks to track it, and use the higher result.</p></li></ul>",
        "statBonusPoints": 0,
        "extraTraining": 0,
        "requiredSpells": [],
        "allowedPerks": [],
        "perkAmount": 0,
